---
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import { recordExample, renderExample, streamExample } from '../../../lib/api-reference.js'

const cliCommands = `node dist/cli.js install
node dist/cli.js doctor
node dist/cli.js render --manifest .suitecut/tour.json --output .suitecut/tour.mp4 --fps 60
node dist/cli.js view https://example.com --executable /absolute/path/to/suitecut-browser
node dist/cli.js --help`

const renderFlags = `node dist/cli.js render --manifest .suitecut/tour.json --output .suitecut/tour.webm \\
  --container webm --width 2560 --height 1440 --fps 60 --quality master \\
  --test-id checkout --retry 1 --failure-mode best-effort --no-narration`

const verifyCommands = `pnpm test
pnpm test:native:cadence
pnpm test:native`
---

<DocsLayout
  title="API and CLI"
  description="Native browser, recording, media and publishing APIs, and the SuiteCut command line."
  section="api"
>
  <h1>Native API and CLI</h1>
  <h2 id="public-exports">Public exports</h2>
  <p>
    <code>suitecut</code> exposes <code>record</code>, <code>defineSuiteCut</code>,
    <code>launchBrowser</code>, <code>createBroadcast</code>, <code>createNativePublisher</code>,
    <code>createNativePage</code>, <code>renderSuiteCut</code> and
    <code>decodeWordTimingArtifact</code>.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>suitecut/native</code>: lower-level sources, recorders and native page APIs.</li>
    <li><code>suitecut/render</code>: the renderer on its own.</li>
    <li><code>suitecut/audio-plugin</code>: helpers for writing speech plugins.</li>
    <li><code>suitecut/types</code>: manifest types.</li>
    <li><code>suitecut/beta</code>: a compatibility alias of the root package.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="recording-options">Recording options</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={recordExample} />
  <p>
    Root recording owns its primary source. <code>recordNative</code> records a caller-owned source. The
    callback context contains the source, page, presentation fixture, cancellation signal and
    <code>addSource</code>. The <code>output</code> option sets a <code>directory</code>,
    <code>manifestPath</code> and <code>pathKind</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="fixture-methods">Fixture methods</h2>
  <p>
    Use <code>selectPage</code>, <code>narrate</code>, <code>checkpoint</code>, <code>hold</code>,
    <code>highlight</code>, <code>zoom</code>, <code>hover</code>, <code>click</code>,
    <code>type</code>, <code>scrollTo</code> and <code>scrollTop</code>. Checkpoints are video
    clips.
  </p>
  <p>
    Highlights come in <code>outline</code>, <code>spotlight</code> and <code>fill</code> modes, with
    optional labels, borders, a backdrop and enter and exit animations.
  </p>

  <h2 id="capture-options">Capture options</h2>
  <p>
    Native launch sets CSS dimensions, device scale 1 or 2, an integer capture rate from 1 to 120
    and BGRA or I420 pixels. Physical frames are bounded to 3840 × 2160. Other launch options
    include
    <code>headless</code>, <code>userDataDir</code>, <code>downloadsPath</code>,
    <code>recordVideo</code>, <code>tracesDir</code>, <code>startupTimeoutMs</code> and
    <code>frameTransport</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Recording capture sets output size and frame rate, a narration tail and boolean page audio.
    Evaluation requires JSON-serializable values.
  </p>

  <h2 id="native-page">Native page</h2>
  <p>
    <code>NativePage</code> provides CSS, role, text, label, placeholder and test-id locators, frames
    and frame locators, keyboard and pointer input, file uploads, network routing, popups, downloads,
    dialogs, screenshots, PDFs and lifecycle events. <code>suitecut/native</code> also exports tracing,
    coverage, HAR record and replay, virtual time, workers and API request contexts.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each family has scoped evidence and known gaps in the
    <a href="https://github.com/skyaara/suitecut/blob/main/docs/playwright-feature-parity.md"
      >feature checklist</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2 id="render-api">Renderer</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={renderExample} />
  <p>
    Beyond size, frame rate and quality, the renderer accepts a container, video and audio codecs,
    pixel format, color range, <code>resultHoldMs</code>, <code>backgroundColor</code>,
    <code>failureMode</code>, narration and source-audio switches, and a <code>selection</code> of test
    and retry. Output rates can be fractional, such as 29.97.
  </p>

  <h2 id="audio-plugin-api">Audio plugins</h2>
  <p>
    Configure local model providers with <code>audioPlugins</code>. The worker invokes
    <code>synthesize</code> and expects mono PCM WAV at the supplied output path.
  </p>

  <h2 id="action-zoom">Action zoom</h2>
  <p>
    Authored zoom is applied by the final renderer. Browser-rendered effects can appear in
    simultaneous broadcasts, but offline zoom and narration mixing don't affect them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="stream-options">Streaming API</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={streamExample} />
  <p>
    <code>createBroadcast</code> uses a fixed bitrate. <code>createNativePublisher</code> is the lower-level
    publisher, with explicit codecs and containers.
  </p>

  <h2 id="word-timings">Word timings</h2>
  <p>
    Built-in Kokoro returns word timings, saved as an artifact for caption highlighting and
    validated against the text and the measured clip duration. The macOS voice and audio plugins
    don't produce word timings. <code>decodeWordTimingArtifact</code> reads the artifact.
  </p>

  <h2 id="command-line-flags">Command line</h2>
  <p>
    Installed packages run the same commands as <code>suitecut install</code>,
    <code>suitecut doctor</code>, <code>suitecut render</code> and <code>suitecut view</code>.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock label="Terminal" code={cliCommands} />
  <p>
    <code>render</code> also accepts <code>--test-id</code>, <code>--retry</code>,
    <code>--container</code>, <code>--video-codec</code>, <code>--audio-codec</code>,
    <code>--pixel-format</code>, <code>--color-range</code>, <code>--width</code>,
    <code>--height</code>, <code>--quality</code>, <code>--result-hold-ms</code>,
    <code>--background-color</code>, <code>--failure-mode</code>, <code>--ffmpeg-path</code> and
    <code>--no-narration</code>.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock label="Terminal" code={renderFlags} />
  <p>
    The package also installs <code>suitecut-test</code>, a native test runner with filtering,
    projects, workers, sharding, repeat-each and JSON, JUnit and HTML reports.
  </p>

  <h2 id="verification">Verification</h2>
  <p>
    Unit tests and decoded cadence checks run without CEF. Real browser verifiers need the built CEF
    executable in <code>SUITECUT_NATIVE_EXECUTABLE</code>.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock label="Terminal" code={verifyCommands} />
</DocsLayout>
